  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ankita Rathore vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 22 October, 2024 Author: Vishal Dhagat Bench: Vishal Dhagat 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Wp No. 27565 of 2024 (Ankita Rathore And Others Vs The State Of Madhya Prad Dated : 22-10-2024 Shri Amanulla Usmani - Advocate for the petitioners.",
    "facts": "It is submitted that he is no longer interested to prosecute writ petition on behalf of petitioners. 5. Petitioners No.1 and 2 submitted that they want to marry each other . They are known to each other for last four years and in live-in relationship for last one year. It is submitted by them that they be granted police protection otherwise petitioner No.1 may be abducted by their family 2 WP-27565-2024 members. Even if the marriage is registered under the Special Marriage Act, the marriage would be no more a valid marriage and it would be an irregular (fasid) marriage.\"",
    "arguments": "They are not able to do their job. There is threat to their lives and limb. 6. Learned Government Advocate appearing for State submitted that police protection will be provided to petitioners and it will be seen that no harm is caused to life and limb of petitioners. She is not permitted to meet her parents. It is further submitted Ankita Rathore vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 22 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/31250953/ 1 that she may not be kept in company of petitioner No.2 and his family members."
  },
